    "updated_at": "2026-11-08T15:10:26Z",
    "body": "Triage note on the open part of this issue, checked on `main` 8f30bee. It's worse than \"expose the Setups page\": in the desktop app a new document can't create a setup at all.\n\n- The only controls that create one, **Create first setup** and **New setup**, are on the Setups page (`pages::setups_page`).\n- The only way to that page is the browser's **Setups** row, and `panes::browser_rows` draws it only once `setup::names` is non-empty, which needs a setup to exist first.\n- The ribbon's Setup group is `[Stock, Origin, Tools, Machine]`, with no Setups cell, and no shortcut targets `UiTarget::Setups`.\n\nSo a user reaches multiple setups, workholding on the Setups page, the tool list and **Export setup sheets...** only by opening a project that already has a setup. #267's \"I have not seen any setup sheets\" is this. The MCP server has no setup tool either, so an agent can't create one.\n\nThe smallest fix is to draw the **Setups** row whenever the Setup section is open: the page already handles the no-setup case (\"No setups in this document ... Create first setup\"). That changes the default browser, so the three shell pixel snapshots move and need regenerating on the CI platform (#255). A ribbon cell would move them too.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
